# MATB Imperative Task API Contract

The four MATB tasks and `SystemHealth` are `forwardRef` components that expose imperative methods
via `useImperativeHandle`. `services/EventService.js` (singleton scheduler) and `src/App.js`
call these methods by name. **Do not rename or remove them.**

## Required method surface

| Component | Imperative methods |
|---|---|
| `MonitoringTask` | `triggerMultipleEvents`, `resetTask`, `togglePause`, `setPause`, `isPaused` |
| `TrackingTask` | `forceManualControl`, `resetTask` |
| `CommunicationsTask` | `triggerCall`, `isActiveMessage`, `getActiveMessageAge`, `clearActiveMessage`, `resetTask` |
| `ResourceManagementTask` | `triggerMultiplePumpFailures`, `setFuelLossRate`, `resetTask` |
| `SystemHealth` | `getHealth`, `resetHealth`, `applyDiscretePenalty` |

## When editing these files

- Preserve the exact method names and their argument object shape (`{callType, responseWindow, ...}`).
- If you genuinely need to change a method signature, update **all call sites** in `EventService.js`
  and `App.js` in the same change and note it in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- New event types should extend the existing switch/dispatch in `EventService.js`, not bypass it.
- `resetTask()` must fully restore initial state (tanks, gauges, audio queue, cursor) — it is called
  on every mode start and on `Ctrl+Q` exit.
